# LAN-first frontend environment template.
# Copy to frontend/.env.local once, then switch between LAN and ONLINE by
# commenting/uncommenting the blocks below. Update the LAN IPs when Wi-Fi changes.
#
# ============================ LAN MODE =============================
NEXT_PUBLIC_EXAM_MODE=LAN
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://10.29.139.67:8080
ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS=10.210.254.230:3000
#
# ========================== ONLINE MODE ============================
# To use the hosted backend, comment the three active LAN lines above and
# uncomment the following three lines:
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_EXAM_MODE=ONLINE
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://quiz-app-s033.onrender.com
# ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS=localhost:3000
#
# NOTES:
# - NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL is the Spring Boot backend address.
# - ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS is the origin clients use to open Next.js in dev mode.
# - Do not use 0.0.0.0 for ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS; it is only a bind address.
# - Keep only one active value for each variable.
# - Restart Next.js after changing .env.local; rebuild for production.
